# K03 (the author, 2026-10-06; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption): a bare resolved head is its
# application with no written argument, through the same consumer as `H()`, diagnosed at the head and never a free
# input of the method; neighbouring atoms are not its arguments.
# The statement `sizeof()` is sizeof applied to nothing: sizeof's own refusal (it was accepted, declaring a Structure
# named sizeof).
fn: m () int
    sizeof()
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
